{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt host/gambit/yin/yin/repl/host.jolt; sed -n '130,245p' host/gambit/host-statics.ss; cat host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss; ls host/gambit; sed -n '1980,2012p' Makefile; rg -n 'gambit|DATOMWORLD' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bin /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bb.edn | head -70\"","aggregated_output":"(ns jolt.gambit.yin\n  \"The memory and memory-backed DHT compositions for the Gambit terminal.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.repl.main :as main]\n            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n(defn- activate-ffi [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry 'jolt.ffi\n    {'sizeof ffi/sizeof}\n    {'sizeof (vm/primitive-profile 'sizeof :pure [1] #{} :none)}))\n\n(defn- materialize-sha256 [value]\n  (jing/materialize! (store/open :mem) value {:algorithm :sha256}))\n\n(defn- activate-store [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry 'dao.jing.mem\n    {'materialize-sha256 materialize-sha256}\n    {'materialize-sha256\n     (vm/primitive-profile 'materialize-sha256 :pure [1] #{} :none)}))\n\n(def ^:private memory-engine-inputs\n  {:host-modules {'jolt.ffi activate-ffi\n                  'dao.jing.mem activate-store}})\n\n(defn- open-memory [spec _opts]\n  {:index-store (store/open spec)\n   :engine-inputs memory-engine-inputs})\n\n(defn- open-dht []\n  (let [join (requiring-resolve 'dao.space.dht/join)\n        payload-budget (requiring-resolve 'dao.space.dht/payload-budget)\n        local (store/open :mem)\n        node (try\n               (join {:local local})\n               (catch Throwable e\n                 (jing/close! local)\n                 (throw e)))\n        handle (:handle node)]\n    (try\n      {:index-store handle\n       :publication-policy {:max-payload-bytes (payload-budget node)}}\n      (catch Throwable e\n        (jing/close! handle)\n        (throw e)))))\n\n(defn- open-store [spec opts]\n  (if (= spec :dht)\n    (assoc (open-dht) :engine-inputs memory-engine-inputs)\n    (open-memory spec opts)))\n\n(defn- parse-store [arg]\n  (if (= arg \"dht:\")\n    :dht\n    (let [spec (store/parse-arg arg [{:prefix \"dht:\" :label \"dht:\"\n                                     :parse (fn [dir]\n                                              (throw (ex-info\n                                                       \"Gambit supports --index-store dht: with memory backing. Durable dht:<dir> requires Chez.\"\n                                                       {:dir dir})))}])]\n      (when-not (= spec :mem)\n        (throw (ex-info \"The local Gambit session supports --index-store mem or dht:\"\n                        {:store spec})))\n      spec)))\n\n(defn -main [& args]\n  (main/main! args {:composition-spec? #{:mem :dht}\n                    :parse-store-arg parse-store\n                    :open open-store}))\n(ns yin.repl.host\n  \"Host adapter for a local Gambit terminal session.\")\n\n(defn- unavailable [& _]\n  (throw (ex-info \"WebSocket transport is unavailable in the local Gambit session\"\n                  {:kind :unsupported-host})))\n\n(defn websocket\n  ([] (websocket nil))\n  ([_opts]\n   {:connect! unavailable\n    :bind! unavailable\n    :unbind! unavailable\n    :close-host! (fn [] nil)}))\n  ;; answers a zero-argument access and nothing more\n  (let ((v (host-static-ref class member)))\n    (cond ((procedure? v) (apply v args))\n          ((null? args) v)\n          (else (throw-jvm (quote IllegalArgumentException)\n                  (string-append class \"/\" member \" is a static field; it takes no arguments\"))))))\n;; The per-site entry points the shared emitter uses when it has a const pool\n;; (Chez caches in them: host/chez/java/host-static.ss). Here they answer through\n;; the uncached lookups, which is the same answer.\n(define (host-static-site-make) (vector #f))\n(define (host-static-ref-site site class member) (host-static-ref class member))\n(define (host-static-proc-site site class member n)\n  (lambda args (apply host-static-call class member args)))\n(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"host-static-call\" host-static-call)\n(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"host-static-ref\" host-static-ref)\n;; (Class/member) with no arguments is a field read when a field is registered\n;; and a no-arg call otherwise — the analyzer's jolt.host/static-member.\n(def-var! \"jolt.host\" \"static-member\"\n  (lambda (class member)\n    (let ((v (host-static-ref class member)))\n      (if (procedure? v) (v) v))))\n\n;; Two kinds of class exist on this target beyond the shims registered below:\n;; the exception hierarchy, which every core throw site constructs ((new\n;; ClassCastException msg) is what (zero? \"a\") raises), and a deftype/defrecord,\n;; whose type name is a var holding its ctor — the same two arms Chez's host-new\n;; (host-static.ss) takes. The throwable ctors are derived from the ONE\n;; hierarchy in class-hierarchy.ss the way host-static-classes.ss derives them,\n;; so (E. msg), (E. msg cause), (E. cause) and (E.) all build the typed\n;; throwable. Anything else names a class this target has no shim for, and says so.\n(define (gambit-exc-ctor canonical)\n  (lambda args\n    (let* ((a0 (if (pair? args) (car args) jolt-nil))\n           (rest (if (pair? args) (cdr args) '()))\n           (cause (if (pair? rest) (car rest) jolt-nil)))\n      (cond\n        ((string? a0) (jolt-host-throwable canonical a0 cause))\n        ((jolt-nil? a0) (jolt-host-throwable canonical jolt-nil))\n        ;; (E. cause): the message is the cause's toString, as on the JVM\n        ((and (null? rest) (ex-info-map? a0))\n         (jolt-host-throwable canonical (jolt-str-render-one a0) a0))\n        (else (jolt-host-throwable canonical (jolt-str-render-one a0) cause))))))\n(let-values (((keys vals) (hashtable-entries jvm-class-parents)))\n  (vector-for-each\n    (lambda (canonical supers)\n      (when (jch-isa? canonical \"Throwable\")\n        (let ((short (jch-last-segment canonical)))\n          (register-class-ctor! short (gambit-exc-ctor canonical))\n          (unless (string=? short canonical)\n            (register-class-ctor! canonical (gambit-exc-ctor canonical))))))\n    keys vals))\n(define (host-new class . args)\n  (let ((ctor (lookup-class class-ctors-tbl class)))\n    (cond\n      (ctor (apply ctor args))\n      (else\n       (let ((cell (or (var-cell-lookup (chez-current-ns) class)\n                       (var-cell-lookup \"clojure.core\" class))))\n         (if (and cell (var-cell-defined? cell) (procedure? (var-cell-root cell)))\n             (apply (var-cell-root cell) args)\n             (jolt-throw\n               (jolt-host-throwable\n                 \"java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException\"\n                 (string-append \"(new \" class \") is unsupported on the gambit target: \"\n                                \"no shim registers the class (host/gambit/host-statics.ss)\")))))))))\n(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"host-new\" (lambda (c . a) (apply host-new c a)))\n\n;; Constructing a File only wraps the path. Store preflight filesystem\n;; operations are governed by the same C4 boundary as the POSIX file overlay.\n(register-class-ctor! \"java.io.File\"\n  (lambda (path) (make-jhost \"file\" (jolt-need-string path))))\n(register-host-methods! \"file\"\n  (cons (cons \"getPath\" jhost-state)\n        (map (lambda (name)\n               (cons name (lambda (_) (joltffi-public-blocking-raise))))\n             '(\"exists\" \"isDirectory\" \"canWrite\" \"mkdirs\"))))\n\n;; ---- the statics the seed reaches -----------------------------------------------\n;; Each is the member Chez registers in host-static-methods.ss, with the same\n;; body, so a call answers the same on both targets. Long/parseLong is\n;; cl-format's number parser (java-parse.ss carries the throw);\n;; Character/isWhitespace and String/join are clojure.main's; java.lang.Math is\n;; the shared math.ss, included after this file; the clojure.lang.Util family,\n;; MapEntry/create and Murmur3/hashOrdered are the gvec's (clojure/core/60-gvec.clj);\n;; PersistentList/EMPTY the gvec's empty; RT/REQUIRE_LOCK the object\n;; serialized-require locks. The Compiler statics (munge, demunge, eval) are\n;; registered by compile-eval.ss at its load, into the same table.\n(register-class-statics! \"Long\"\n  (list (cons \"parseLong\" (lambda (s . r) (parse-int-or-throw s (if (null? r) 10 (jnum->exact (car r))) \"long\")))))\n;; JVM Character.isWhitespace: Unicode whitespace MINUS the no-break spaces the\n;; JVM excludes (U+00A0/U+2007/U+202F) and NEL (U+0085), plus U+001C..U+001F.\n(register-class-statics! \"Character\"\n  (list (cons \"isWhitespace\" (lambda (c) (let ((cp (char-code c)))\n                                           (or (and (fx>=? cp #x1C) (fx<=? cp #x1F))\n                                               (and (char-whitespace? (integer->char cp))\n                                                    (not (fx=? cp #xA0)) (not (fx=? cp #x2007)) (not (fx=? cp #x202F))\n                                                    (not (fx=? cp #x85)))))))))\n;; String.join(delim, elems) — elems as a collection or spread as varargs\n(register-class-statics! \"String\"\n  (list (cons \"join\" (lambda (delim . parts)\n                       (let ((items (if (and (fx=? (length parts) 1)\n                                             (not (string? (car parts))))\n                                        (seq->list (jolt-seq (car parts)))\n                                        parts)))\n                         (jolt-str-join-strs (map jolt-str-render-one items)\n                                             (jolt-str-render-one delim)))))))\n(let ((util-statics\n       (list (cons \"hash\" (lambda (x) (if (jolt-nil? x) 0 (record-method-dispatch x \"hashCode\" jolt-nil))))\n             (cons \"hasheq\" (lambda (x) (jolt-hash x)))\n             (cons \"equiv\" (lambda (a b) (if (jolt= a b) #t #f)))\n             (cons \"identical\" (lambda (a b) (if (eq? a b) #t #f)))\n             (cons \"compare\" (lambda (a b) (jolt-compare a b)))\n             (cons \"isInteger\" (lambda (x) (if (and (number? x) (exact? x) (integer? x)) #t #f)))\n             (cons \"equals\" (lambda (a b) (if (jolt= a b) #t #f))))))\n  (register-class-statics! \"Util\" util-statics)\n  (register-class-statics! \"clojure.lang.Util\" util-statics))\n#!/usr/bin/env gsi-script\n;; The gate builds the kernel with gsc. App namespaces still load from source.\n;; The Gambit boot omits Chez's external data-reader loader.\n(define data-readers-active #f)\n(load (getenv \"JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT\"))\n(##include \"yin-repl-driver.ss\")\nboot-probe.scm\nboot.ss\nbuild-yin-boot.py\neval-fns.ss\neval-test.ss\neval-twins-check.sh\nffi\ngambitcheck.ss\ngen-boot.ss\ngen-records.ss\ngen-seed.ss\ngen-unicode-nfc.py\nhasheq.ss\nhost-apply.ss\nhost-ffi.ss\nhost-statics.ss\nhost-vars.ss\nkernel-test.ss\nprelude-shims.ss\nprofile-test.ss\nprofiles.ss\nrecords-gambit.ss\nrepl-main.ss\nrt-core.ss\nscheme-adapter-runtime.ss\nseed\nseed-statics-allowlist.txt\nseed-statics.sh\nseed-statics.ss\nsource-loader-test.ss\nsource-loader.ss\nunbound-allowlist.txt\nunbound-check.sh\nunbound-check.ss\nunbound-vars-allowlist.txt\nunbound-vars-lib.ss\nunbound-vars.ss\nunicode-nfc-data.ss\nunicode-nfc.ss\nyin\nyin-repl-driver.ss\nyin-repl-main.ss\nyin-repl-native.ss\n\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 240 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\nDATOMWORLD_ROOT ?= ../datomworld\ngambitdaobytes:\n\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 240 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss \"$(abspath $(DATOMWORLD_ROOT))\"\n\n# The interpreted bootstrap is available through yin-repl-main.ss. Compiling\n# the same boot makes the full app closure fit the acceptance watchdog.\nGAMBIT_YIN_BOOT ?=\ngambityinrepl gambitdht: gambitffi-bridge\n\t@yin_root=\"$(abspath $(DATOMWORLD_ROOT))\"; \\\n\tif [ ! -f \"$$yin_root/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\" ]; then \\\n\t  echo \"$@: no Yin source entry under $$yin_root. Set DATOMWORLD_ROOT to a Datomworld checkout.\" >&2; \\\n\t  exit 2; \\\n\tfi; \\\n\tboot=\"$(GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT)\"; \\\n\tif [ -z \"$$boot\" ]; then \\\n\t  boot=$$(sh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 2400 python3 host/gambit/build-yin-boot.py \\\n\t    \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" \"$(abspath build/gambit-yin)\") || exit $$?; \\\n\tfi; \\\n\tif [ \"$@\" = gambitdht ]; then \\\n\t  sh test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" \"$$boot\"; \\\n\telse \\\n\t  JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=\"$$boot\" sh test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh \\\n\t    \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss; \\\n\tfi\n\n# Every Scheme global the full-profile boot references is defined — Gambit's\n# own linker report over the compiled boot, minus what the record translator\n# evals at runtime, against host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt (untaken paths;\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bb.edn:27:  {:doc \"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt; Lane B: --target chez|gambit, the child reports jolt-target and the driver asserts it fail-closed — the gambit child runs the same smoke form under $JOLT_GAMBIT)\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bb.edn:34:  {:doc \"Run jolt -Srepro -M:jolt with the arguments given (a script path, -e ...), under build/tools/jolt-env.sh (Lane B: --target chez|gambit; a fail-closed identity preflight child runs first, then the arguments pass through unchanged)\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bb.edn:41:  {:doc \"Lane B target-aware launcher smoke: run a trivial child under the requested host scheme through the jolt-launch seam (--target chez, the default, or --target gambit via JOLT_GAMBIT) and fail closed unless the child itself reports jolt-target: <target> (needs bb bootstrap:jolt; the gambit leg needs the mise-pinned gsi)\"\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/bb.edn:53:  {:doc \"J1b: libcrypto provenance (qualified, missing, undeclared, version-floor, wrong-library-first, Linux LD_PRELOAD) and 256 MiB :blocking hash collect-safety, each in a child jolt process (needs bb build:jolt-native; Lane B: --target chez|gambit, fail-closed identity gate, gambit refused — the wrapper protocol is Chez-tier)\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
