{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt; sed -n '1,175p' test/gambit/fixtures/yin-dht-probe.jolt; cat test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh; ls -l /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/tools; ls -la /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.git | head\"","aggregated_output":"959c06c2b96833dbb31a0290acb56ce93b7d44c926bfd4de562fe0fa39d8dc36  host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm\n5b32a1831f98b51d97ff27eaf6ce77d90780480dc2fc6b44a4efeb6b03dae976  host/gambit/ffi/generated-shims.scm\neb94a858c05ea29cd058da27b0e86d168562cf1791441f1b3475b106f257bc64  host/gambit/ffi/shapes.json\n34f53a1e8c3833e2b4b4b42ca82bfa58646f8f6eb160f1b32692a416a24bb036  host/gambit/ffi/generate-shims.py\n50e9b9c24123206070d08a72ed531666d98053e0d1684b8862513758146d4b6c  host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture.c\nd2959a1ba04099845f391dcc599168ec5b38c43d0146c1e8c06a142729721b3c  host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture2.c\n4b53e1e971da4b1ea3705e7b8a203b6db278fc3de5bec8bce6ac1c5dce573ced  host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-dep.c\n9864b13612a918a8f02d102904cb983a79ef18531a234ee8bf5ef4c27ce1ce0a  host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-unloadable.c\n18356bf2d1180c5b71b79a43f08523980e819994bf718832c1b89e9fd07b74a7  host/gambit/ffi/toolchain.py\na43734c2b9d56c6e7e480fb4e763f6c8709f7e4fb6ed9406aee4457680c7eb93  host/gambit/ffi/record-toolchain.sh\n1dbce807b67cb75eb28305f95b940d94244f7e7c0b5076baafc6d27a8f037e5e  host/gambit/ffi/verify-toolchain.sh\nc3b94d7612453079ffbf77291780519f2f9f25f44cb8dd997bf07af302a90e77  host/gambit/ffi/verify-digests.sh\n16ff5a1314ba63963db5380f9699e74515ed46e202a377340f5da31dc4ec380e  host/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh\n;; Appended to a scratch copy of jolt.gambit.yin. Keep the real driver and\n;; launcher composition so each attempted operation gets its own Yin reply.\n(require '[dao.stream :as p1e-stream]\n         '[dao.stream.ringbuffer :as p1e-ring]\n         '[jolt.scheme :as p1e-scheme])\n\n(def ^:private p1e-var (p1e-scheme/proc \"var-deref\"))\n(def ^:private p1e-dir (jolt.host/getenv \"JOLT_P1E_STORE\"))\n(def ^:private p1e-durable (atom nil))\n(def ^:private p1e-memory (atom nil))\n(def ^:private p1e-session-store (atom nil))\n(def ^:private p1e-requests (atom nil))\n(def ^:private p1e-value {:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\" :count 3})\n\n(defn- p1e-call [namespace var-name & args]\n  ;; Defer each dependency so a failed load becomes a reply at the prompt.\n  (require (symbol namespace))\n  (apply (p1e-var namespace var-name) args))\n\n(defn- p1e-make-ring []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (p1e-ring/create! {:dao.stream/type p1e-ring/transport-type\n                      p1e-ring/capacity-key 8})))\n\n(defn- p1e-next [ring cursor]\n  (p1e-stream/next ring (:dao.stream/cursor cursor)))\n\n(defn- p1e-open-shell []\n  (let [opened (p1e-call \"yin.shell.store\" \"open\" {:type :dht :dir p1e-dir} {})]\n    (reset! p1e-durable (:index-store opened))\n    :durable-dht-opened))\n\n(defn- p1e-open-dir []\n  (let [handle (p1e-call \"dao.space.store\" \"open\" p1e-dir)]\n    (jing/close! handle)\n    :durable-directory-opened))\n\n(defn- p1e-open-memory []\n  (let [requests (p1e-make-ring)\n        handle (p1e-call \"dao.jing.dht\" \"store-handle\"\n                         {:local (store/open :mem) :requests requests})]\n    (reset! p1e-memory handle)\n    (reset! p1e-requests requests)\n    :memory-dht-handle-opened))\n\n(defn- p1e-check-request []\n  (let [requests @p1e-requests\n        result (p1e-next requests (p1e-stream/cursor requests :dao.stream/oldest))]\n    (:dao.stream/value result)))\n\n(defn- p1e-loopback []\n  (let [traffic (p1e-make-ring)\n        cursor (p1e-stream/cursor traffic :dao.stream/oldest)\n        seam (p1e-call \"dao.stream.udp\" \"bind!\"\n                       {:identity \"p1e-loopback\" :deposit traffic\n                        :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\" :bind-port 0})]\n    (try\n      (let [bound (p1e-next traffic cursor)\n            local (get-in bound [:dao.stream/value :dao.stream.datagram/local])\n            port (:dao.stream.datagram/port local)\n            payload (byte-array [42 -1 0])]\n        (when-not (and (= \"127.0.0.1\" (:dao.stream.datagram/host local))\n                       (integer? port) (pos? port))\n          (throw (ex-info \"UDP loopback did not bind\" {:bound bound})))\n        (let [sent ((:send! seam) \"127.0.0.1\" port payload)\n              received (loop [attempts 16]\n                         (let [step ((:step! seam))\n                               rx (p1e-next traffic bound)]\n                           (if (or (:progressed? step) (zero? attempts))\n                             rx\n                             (recur (dec attempts)))))\n              packet (:dao.stream/value received)]\n          ((:close! seam))\n          (let [closed (:dao.stream/value (p1e-next traffic received))]\n            (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome sent))\n                     (= \"Kv8A\" (:dao.stream.datagram/bytes packet))\n                     (= local (:dao.stream.datagram/source packet))\n                     (= :dao.stream.datagram/closed (:dao.stream.datagram/event closed)))\n              [:udp-loopback-ok (:dao.stream.datagram/bytes packet) :closed]\n              (throw (ex-info \"UDP loopback did not round trip\"\n                              {:sent sent :packet packet :closed closed}))))))\n      (finally\n        ((:close! seam))))))\n\n(defn- p1e-session-round-trip []\n  (let [handle @p1e-session-store\n        address (jing/segment-key p1e-value)]\n    (when (and handle\n               (= :missing (jing/get handle address :missing))\n               (= address (jing/materialize! handle p1e-value))\n               (= p1e-value (jing/get handle address :missing)))\n      [:dht-index-put-get address p1e-value])))\n\n(defn- p1e-run [op]\n  (case op\n    :shell-open (p1e-open-shell)\n    :durable-put (if-let [handle @p1e-durable]\n                   (jing/materialize! handle p1e-value)\n                   :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle)\n    :durable-get (if-let [handle @p1e-durable]\n                   (jing/get handle (jing/segment-key p1e-value) :missing)\n                   :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle)\n    :directory-open (p1e-open-dir)\n    :memory-open (p1e-open-memory)\n    :memory-put (if-let [handle @p1e-memory]\n                  (jing/materialize! handle p1e-value)\n                  :blocked-no-memory-dht-handle)\n    :memory-get (if-let [handle @p1e-memory]\n                  (jing/get handle (jing/segment-key p1e-value) :missing)\n                  :blocked-no-memory-dht-handle)\n    :replicate-request (= (jing/segment-key p1e-value)\n                          (:dao.jing.dht/replicate (p1e-check-request)))\n    :session-round-trip (p1e-session-round-trip)\n    :udp-loopback (p1e-loopback)\n    :udp-native-load (do (require 'jolt.socket.native) :socket-native-loaded)\n    :c4-control (p1e-call \"dao.posix.file\" \"realpath\" p1e-dir)\n    :close (do (jing/close! @p1e-durable) (jing/close! @p1e-memory) :closed)))\n\n(defn- p1e-activate [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry 'p1e.probe\n    {'run p1e-run}\n    {'run (vm/primitive-profile 'run :pure [1] #{} :none)}))\n\n(defn- p1e-open [spec opts]\n  (let [opened (open-store spec opts)]\n    (when (= :dht spec)\n      (reset! p1e-session-store (:index-store opened)))\n    (assoc-in opened [:engine-inputs :host-modules 'p1e.probe] p1e-activate)))\n\n(defn -main [& args]\n  (main/main! args {:composition-spec? #{:mem :dht}\n                    :parse-store-arg parse-store\n                    :open p1e-open}))\n#!/bin/sh\n# Run the stock launcher and the same composition with a diagnostic host module.\n# Arguments are absolute paths. Build the bridge and compiled boot first.\nset -eu\n\ngsi=$1\ndatomworld=$2\nexport JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=$3\nmode=${4:-both}\nexport JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE=1\nrepo=$(CDPATH='' cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")/../..\" && pwd)\ncd \"$repo\"\nmkdir -p build/gambit-dht\nrun=$(mktemp -d \"$repo/build/gambit-dht/run.XXXXXX\")\necho \"gambitdht receipts: $run\"\nmkdir \"$run/store\"\nexport JOLT_P1E_STORE=\"$run/store\"\n\nsession() {\n  name=$1\n  status=0\n  started=$(date +%s)\n  sh \"$repo/host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh\" \"${GAMBIT_DHT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-2400}\" \\\n    \"$gsi\" \"$repo/host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss\" \"$datomworld\" \\\n    --no-state --index-store dht: >\"$run/$name.stdout\" 2>\"$run/$name.stderr\" || status=$?\n  echo \"$status\" >\"$run/$name.status\"\n  cat \"$run/$name.stdout\"\n  echo \"$name launcher exit $status ($(($(date +%s) - started))s)\"\n  if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then\n    tail -30 \"$run/$name.stderr\" >&2\n    return \"$status\"\n  fi\n}\n\nstock() {\n  session stock <<'FORMS'\n(+ 20 22)\n(quit)\nFORMS\n  grep -Fx 'yin> 42' \"$run/stock.stdout\" >/dev/null\n  grep -Fx 'yin> Bye' \"$run/stock.stdout\" >/dev/null\n  test \"$(grep -c '^yin> ' \"$run/stock.stdout\")\" -eq 2\n  grep -E 'ready dao[.]space[.]dht$' \"$run/stock.stderr\" >/dev/null\n  echo \"gambitdht: PASS — stock launcher opened dht: and quit\"\n}\n\ndiagnostics() {\n  # Extend the session's host modules. The same native launcher and open-store\n  # path initialize the session, and the fixture observes its actual handle.\n  overlay=\"$run/jolt\"\n  mkdir -p \"$overlay/host/gambit\"\n  cp -R \"$repo/host/gambit/yin\" \"$overlay/host/gambit/yin\"\n  cat \"$repo/test/gambit/fixtures/yin-dht-probe.jolt\" >>\"$overlay/host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt\"\n  for name in build stdlib jolt-core; do\n    ln -s \"$repo/$name\" \"$overlay/$name\"\n  done\n  cd \"$overlay\"\n\n  session diagnostics <<'FORMS'\n(+ 20 22)\n(require 'p1e.probe)\n(p1e.probe/run :session-round-trip)\n(p1e.probe/run :shell-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :durable-put)\n(p1e.probe/run :durable-get)\n(p1e.probe/run :directory-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-put)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-get)\n(p1e.probe/run :replicate-request)\n(p1e.probe/run :udp-loopback)\n(p1e.probe/run :udp-native-load)\n(p1e.probe/run :c4-control)\n(p1e.probe/run :close)\n(+ 40 3)\n(quit)\nFORMS\n\n  awk '\n    /^yin> 42$/ && step == 0 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\047p1e[.]probe$/ && step == 1 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\[ *:dht-index-put-get :segment\\/blake3-[0-9a-f]+ \\{:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3\\} *\\]$/ && step == 2 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 3 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle$/ && (step == 4 || step == 5) { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 6 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :memory-dht-handle-opened$/ && step == 7 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :segment\\/blake3-[0-9a-f]+$/ && step == 8 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\{:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3\\}$/ && step == 9 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> true$/ && step == 10 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\[ *:udp-loopback-ok \"Kv8A\" :closed *\\]$/ && step == 11 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :socket-native-loaded$/ && step == 12 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 13 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :closed$/ && step == 14 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> 43$/ && step == 15 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Bye$/ && step == 16 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> / { unexpected = 1 }\n    END { exit !(step == 17 && !unexpected) }\n  ' \"$run/diagnostics.stdout\" || {\n    echo \"gambitdht: the probe did not produce the expected replies\" >&2\n    exit 1\n  }\n  test -z \"$(ls -A \"$JOLT_P1E_STORE\")\"\n  echo \"gambitdht: PASS — selected DHT index put/get, portable replication request, UDP loopback and close, C4 refusals, clean quit\"\n}\n\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  stock) stock ;;\n  diagnostics) diagnostics ;;\n  both) stock; diagnostics ;;\n  *) echo \"usage: $0 GSI DATOMWORLD_ROOT BOOT [stock|diagnostics|both]\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\nesac\ntotal 16\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 37 sto  staff  1184 Nov 20 09:36 jolt\n-rw-r--r--@  1 sto  staff   385 Nov 20 09:36 jolt-env.sh\n-rw-r--r--@  1 sto  staff   200 Nov 20 09:36 jolt-patches.edn\ntotal 3544\ndrwxr-xr-x   25 sto  staff      800 Nov 26 18:14 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  87 sto  staff     2784 Nov 26 18:00 ..\n-rw-r--r--@   1 sto  staff      296 Nov 26 18:05 COMMIT_EDITMSG\n-rw-r--r--@   1 sto  staff    16623 Nov 21 18:50 COMMIT_EDITMSG~\n-rw-r--r--@   1 sto  staff    26279 Nov 26 18:14 FETCH_HEAD\n-rw-r--r--@   1 sto  staff       23 Nov 26 18:00 HEAD\n-rw-r--r--@   1 sto  staff       41 Nov 26 18:00 ORIG_HEAD\n-rw-r--r--@   1 sto  staff     5013 Nov 24 15:04 config\n-rw-r--r--    1 sto  staff       73 Mar 19  2022 description\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'jolt.*(bytevector|u8vector)|bytevector.*jolt' host/gambit/yin host/gambit/host-vars.ss host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss host/chez/natives-array.ss; find /Users/sto -maxdepth 5 -type d -name 'gambit*' 2>/dev/null | head -35; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '14999,15030p;15738,15771p;17204,17237p;18058,18112p;18121,18150p' /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/doc/gambit.html; rg -ni 'port.*file.descriptor|file.lock|lock-file|last-os-error|os-exception-code|create-directory|file.permissions|rename-file' /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/doc/gambit.html | head -46; find /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8 -name _io.scm; ls -l /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1f/vendor/irregex/irregex.scm\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '14999,15030p;15738,15771p;17204,17237p;18058,18112p;18121,18150p' /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/doc/gambit.html; rg -ni 'port.*file.descriptor|file.lock|lock-file|last-os-error|os-exception-code|create-directory|file.permissions|rename-file' /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/doc/gambit.html | head -46; find /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8 -name _io.scm; ls -l /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1f/vendor/irregex/irregex.scm\"","aggregated_output":"<a name=\"Definition_of_path-normalize\"></a><a name=\"Procedure_path-normalize\"></a><a name=\"index-path_002dnormalize\"></a><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"> <code>(</code><code><b><a href=\"https://github.com/gambit/gambit/wiki/Documentation:Procedure%20path%E2%80%90normalize\">path-normalize</a></b></code><i> <var>path</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>allow-relative?</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>origin-directory</var><span class=\"roman\">]</span><span class=\"roman\">]</span></i><code>)</code></td><td align=\"right\">procedure</td></tr></table>\n\n<a name=\"index-normalized-path\"></a>\n<p>The procedure <code>path-normalize</code> takes a path of a file or\ndirectory and returns its normalized path.  The optional\n<var>origin-directory</var> parameter, which defaults to the current\nworking directory, is the directory used to resolve relative paths.\nAll components of the paths <var>path</var> and\n<var>origin-directory</var> must exist, except possibly the last\ncomponent of <var>path</var>.  A normalized path is a path\ncontaining no redundant parts and which is consistent with the current\nstructure of the filesystem.  A normalized path of a directory will\nalways end with a path separator (i.e. &lsquo;<samp>/</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp>\\</samp>&rsquo;, or &lsquo;<samp>:</samp>&rsquo;\ndepending on the operating system).  The optional\n<var>allow-relative?</var> parameter, which defaults to <code>#f</code>,\nindicates if the path returned can be expressed relatively to\n<var>origin-directory</var>: a <code>#f</code> requests an absolute path,\nthe symbol <code>shortest</code> requests the shortest of the absolute and\nrelative paths, and any other value requests the relative path.  The\nshortest path is useful for interaction with the user because short\nrelative paths are typically easier to read than long absolute paths.\n</p>\n<p>For example under UNIX:\n</p>\n<table><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td><pre class=\"smallexample\">&gt; <b>(path-expand &quot;../foo&quot;)</b>\n&quot;/Users/feeley/gambit/doc/../foo&quot;\n&gt; <b>(path-normalize &quot;../foo&quot;)</b>\n&quot;/Users/feeley/gambit/foo&quot;\n&gt; <b>(path-normalize &quot;this/file/does/not/exist&quot;)</b>\n*** ERROR IN (console)@3.1 -- No such file or directory\n(path-normalize &quot;this/file/does/not/exist&quot;)\n</pre></td></tr></table>\n<a name=\"Definition_of_file-info-type\"></a><a name=\"Procedure_file-info-type\"></a><a name=\"index-file_002dinfo_002dtype\"></a><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"> <code>(</code><code><b><a href=\"https://github.com/gambit/gambit/wiki/Documentation:Procedure%20file%E2%80%90info%E2%80%90type\">file-info-type</a></b></code><i> <var>file-info</var></i><code>)</code></td><td align=\"right\">procedure</td></tr></table>\n\n<p>Returns the type field of the file-information record\n<var>file-info</var>.  The type is denoted by a symbol.\nThe following types are possible:\n</p>\n<dl compact=\"compact\">\n<dt> <code>regular</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Regular file\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>directory</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Directory\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>character-special</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Character special device\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>block-special</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Block special device\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>fifo</code></dt>\n<dd><p>FIFO\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>symbolic-link</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Symbolic link\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>socket</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Socket\n</p></dd>\n<dt> <code>unknown</code></dt>\n<dd><p>File is of an unknown type\n</p></dd>\n</dl>\n\n<p>For example:\n<a name=\"Definition_of_force-output\"></a><a name=\"Procedure_force-output\"></a><a name=\"index-force_002doutput\"></a><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"> <code>(</code><code><b><a href=\"https://github.com/gambit/gambit/wiki/Documentation:Procedure%20force%E2%80%90output\">force-output</a></b></code><i> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>port</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>level</var><span class=\"roman\">]</span><span class=\"roman\">]</span></i><code>)</code></td><td align=\"right\">procedure</td></tr></table>\n\n<p>The procedure <code>force-output</code> causes the data that was written to\nthe output-port <var>port</var> to be moved closer to its destination\naccording to <var>level</var>, an exact integer in the range 0 to 2.  If\n<var>port</var> is not specified, the current output-port is used.  If\n<var>level</var> is not specified, it defaults to 0.  Values of <var>level</var>\nabove 0 are equivalent to <var>level</var> = 0 except for device ports as\nexplained below.\n</p>\n<p>When <var>level</var> is 0, the output buffers of <var>port</var> which are\nmanaged in the Scheme process are drained (i.e.  the output operation\nthat was delayed due to buffering is actually performed).  In the case\nof a device port the data is passed to the operating system and it\nbecomes its responsibility to transmit the data to the device.  The\noperating system may implement its own buffering approach which delays\nthe transmission of the data to the device.\n</p>\n<p>When <var>level</var> is 1, in addition to the operations for <var>level</var> =\n0 and if the operating system supports the functionality, the\noperating system is requested to transmit the data to the device.  On\nUNIX this corresponds to a <code>fsync</code> system call.\n</p>\n<p>When <var>level</var> is 2, in addition to the operations for <var>level</var> =\n1 and if the operating system supports the functionality, the\noperating system is requested to wait until the device reports that\nthe data was saved by the device (e.g. actually written to disk in the\ncase of a file).  This operation can take a long time on some\noperating systems.  On macOS this corresponds to a <code>fcntl</code>\nsystem call with operation <code>F_FULLFSYNC</code>.\n</p>\n<p>For example:\n</p>\n<table><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td><pre class=\"smallexample\">&gt; <b>(define p (open-tcp-client &quot;www.iro.umontreal.ca:80&quot;))</b>\n</p>\n<p>The first argument of these procedures is either a string denoting a\nfilesystem path or a list of port settings which must contain a\n<code>path:</code> setting.  Here are the settings allowed in addition to\nthe generic settings of byte-ports:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<code>path:</code> <var>string</var>\n\n<p>This setting indicates the location of the file in the filesystem.\nThere is no default value for this setting.\n</p>\n</li><li>\n<code>append:</code> ( <code>#f</code> | <code>#t</code> )\n\n<p>This setting controls whether output will be added to the end of the\nfile.  This is useful for writing to log files that might be open by\nmore than one process.  The default value of this setting is\n<code>#f</code>.\n</p>\n</li><li>\n<code>create:</code> ( <code>#f</code> | <code>#t</code> | <code>maybe</code> )\n\n<p>This setting controls whether the file will be created when it is\nopened.  A setting of <code>#f</code> requires that the file exist\n(otherwise an exception is raised).  A setting of <code>#t</code> requires\nthat the file does not exist (otherwise an exception is raised).  A\nsetting of <code>maybe</code> will create the file if it does not exist.\nThe default value of this setting is <code>maybe</code> for output-ports and\n<code>#f</code> for input-ports and bidirectional ports.\n</p>\n</li><li>\n<code>permissions:</code> <var>12-bit-exact-integer</var>\n\n<p>This setting controls the UNIX permissions that will be attached to\nthe file if it is created.  The default value of this setting is\n<code>#o666</code>.\n</p>\n</li><li>\n<code>truncate:</code> ( <code>#f</code> | <code>#t</code> )\n\n<p>This setting controls whether the file will be truncated when it is\nopened.  For input-ports and bidirectional ports, the default value of\nthis setting is <code>#f</code>.  For output-ports, the default value of\nthis setting is <code>#t</code> when the <code>append:</code> setting is <code>#f</code>,\nand <code>#f</code> otherwise.\n</p>\n</li></ul>\n\n<p>For example:\n</p>\n<table><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td><pre class=\"smallexample\">&gt; <b>(with-output-to-file\n    (list path: &quot;nofile&quot;\n          create: #f)\n<a name=\"Definition_of_input-port-byte-position\"></a><a name=\"Procedure_input-port-byte-position\"></a><a name=\"index-input_002dport_002dbyte_002dposition\"></a><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"> <code>(</code><code><b><a href=\"https://github.com/gambit/gambit/wiki/Documentation:Procedure%20input%E2%80%90port%E2%80%90byte%E2%80%90position\">input-port-byte-position</a></b></code><i> <var>port</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>position</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>whence</var><span class=\"roman\">]</span><span class=\"roman\">]</span></i><code>)</code></td><td align=\"right\">procedure</td></tr></table>\n<a name=\"Definition_of_output-port-byte-position\"></a><a name=\"Procedure_output-port-byte-position\"></a><a name=\"index-output_002dport_002dbyte_002dposition\"></a><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"> <code>(</code><code><b><a href=\"https://github.com/gambit/gambit/wiki/Documentation:Procedure%20output%E2%80%90port%E2%80%90byte%E2%80%90position\">output-port-byte-position</a></b></code><i> <var>port</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>position</var> <span class=\"roman\">[</span><var>whence</var><span class=\"roman\">]</span><span class=\"roman\">]</span></i><code>)</code></td><td align=\"right\">procedure</td></tr></table>\n\n<p>When called with a single argument these procedures return the byte\nposition where the next I/O operation would take place in the file\nattached to the given <var>port</var> (relative to the beginning of the\nfile).  When called with two or three arguments, the byte position for\nsubsequent I/O operations on the given <var>port</var> is changed to\n<var>position</var>, which must be an exact integer.  When <var>whence</var> is\nomitted or is 0, the <var>position</var> is relative to the beginning of\nthe file.  When <var>whence</var> is 1, the <var>position</var> is relative to\nthe current byte position of the file.  When <var>whence</var> is 2, the\n<var>position</var> is relative to the end of the file.  The return value\nis the new byte position.  On most operating systems the byte position\nfor reading and writing of a given bidirectional port are the same.\n</p>\n<p>When <code>input-port-byte-position</code> is called to change the byte\nposition of an input-port, all input buffers will be flushed so that\nthe next byte read will be the one at the given position.\n</p>\n<p>When <code>output-port-byte-position</code> is called to change the byte\nposition of an output-port, there is an implicit call to\n<code>force-output</code> before the position is changed.\n</p>\n<p>For example:\n</p>\n<table><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td><pre class=\"smallexample\">&gt; <b>(define p  <span class=\"roman\"><i>; p is an input-output-port</i></span>\n    (open-file '(path: &quot;test&quot; char-encoding: ISO-8859-1 create: maybe)))</b>\n&gt; <b>(list (input-port-byte-position p) (output-port-byte-position p))</b>\n(0 0)\n13434:<a name=\"Definition_of_os-exception-code\"></a><a name=\"Procedure_os-exception-code\"></a><a name=\"index-os_002dexception_002dcode\"></a><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td align=\"left\"> <code>(</code><code><b><a href=\"https://github.com/gambit/gambit/wiki/Documenta