{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yin/shell/store.cljc; sed -n '260,315p;695,759p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '255,315p;335,407p' src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc; rg -n '\"'^('\"\\\\(def|   \\\\[)' src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc | head -37; sed -n '1358,1415p' src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc; rg -n 'lock|sync|truncate|open_read' native/jolt-file/jolt_file.c\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.shell.store\n  \"The composition's store-selection factory\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\n\n   The engine's own selection (`yin.repl.store`) knows two stores —\n   `mem` and `file:<dir>` — and answers a generic `dao.jing` content\n   handle for each.  Every storage implementation past those two is a\n   composition's: it owns the scheme, the checked spec, the open, and the\n   transport state the open produces.  This namespace is that factory for\n   the shell compositions, so a host entry point resolves one\n   `--index-store` value against one table instead of asking the engine\n   about a backend the engine must never name.\n\n   It owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock or namespace global:\n   selection is a pure dispatch, and the state an open produces is\n   answered as two separate values — the engine's handle and the\n   composition's node — never as one handle with a node inside it.\"\n  (:require [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.shell.dht :as shell.dht]\n            [yin.shell.query :as shell.query]\n            [yin.shell.session :as session]))\n\n\n(def dht-scheme\n  \"The store scheme the DHT composition registers with the engine's\n   parser, as plain data: a prefix to match, a label for the refusal and\n   help text, and a directory-to-spec projection.  The engine matches the\n   prefix and calls `:parse`; it never learns what the answer means.\"\n  {:prefix shell.dht/dht-scheme\n   :label (str shell.dht/dht-scheme \"<dir>\")\n   :type :dht\n   :parse (fn [dir] {:type :dht :dir dir})})\n\n\n(def schemes\n  \"Every scheme this factory adds to the engine's own two, in the order\n   the parser tries them.\"\n  [dht-scheme])\n\n\n(defn parse-arg\n  \"The `--index-store` value as a spec, over the engine's two schemes and\n   `schemes`: `:mem`, `{:type :file :dir dir}`, or `{:type :dht :dir\n   dir}`.  A missing value, an unknown scheme and an empty directory are\n   refused with every supported form named, so the refusal an operator\n   reads lists the composition's stores too.\"\n  [value]\n  (store/parse-arg value schemes))\n\n\n(defn composition-spec?\n  \"True when `spec` names a store a composition opens rather than one the\n   engine's own selection does.\"\n  [spec]\n  (boolean (and (map? spec)\n                (some #(= (:type %) (:type spec)) schemes))))\n\n\n(defn checked-spec\n  \"Validate an `:index-store-spec` over both selections: the engine's own\n   `:mem` and `{:type :file :dir dir}`, and each registered composition's\n   own checked spec.  Anything else is refused with its reason.\"\n  [spec]\n  (if (composition-spec? spec)\n    (shell.dht/checked-spec spec)\n    (store/checked-spec spec)))\n\n\n(defn open\n  \"Open the store `spec` names, answering the two values of section 3's\n   ownership split:\n\n   ```clojure\n   {:index-store <the generic dao.jing handle the engine is constructed\n                  with>\n    :node <the composition's transport step-owner value, or nil for a\n           store with no transport>\n    :recovery <what the open validated, or nil>\n    :publication-policy <the immutable generic policy of section 5, or nil>\n    :retain-index-on-reset? bool}\n   ```\n\n   `opts` reaches the composition that opens.  They are either its own\n   names (`yin.shell.dht/open`'s `:key`, `:ws`, `:write-heads!`,\n   `:open-store`) or the host driver's neutral ones (`:publisher-key`,\n   `:ws-host`), translated here, so an engine entry point never learns what\n   a composition calls its own inputs.  `:principals`, `:admission` and\n   `:name-env` join the prepared `:link-source` of `:engine-inputs`: the\n   further `yin.repl/create-state` options this composition injects, so a\n   `(reset)` or a `(vm ...)` rebuild reconstructs a session that still\n   resolves signed names and still serves the composition's modules.\n   `:session` is the transport half of the composition session\n   (`yin.shell.session/transport-state`), which a host carries beside its\n   engine value and never inside it.\n\n   A refusal releases whatever the failed open acquired, exactly once, and\n   propagates as itself.\n\n   The engine is handed `:index-store` and never `:node`; the composition\n   keeps the node and steps it\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n  ([spec opts]\n   (if (composition-spec? spec)\n     (let [_ (when (or (:content-store opts) (:content-client opts))\n               (throw (ex-info \"A composed store cannot use a second content source\"\n                               {:index-store-spec spec})))\n           key (or (:key opts) (:publisher-key opts))\n           opened (shell.dht/open spec {:key key\n                                        :ws (or (:ws opts) (:ws-host opts))\n                                        :write-heads! (:write-heads! opts)\n                                        :open-store (:open-store opts)})]\n       (assoc opened\n              :engine-inputs\n              {:link-source (shell.dht/link-source\n                              spec\n                              {:key key\n                               :principals (:principals opts)\n                               :admission (get opts :admission {})\n                               :name-env (:name-env opts)})\n               :host-modules shell.query/registrations}\n              :session (session/transport-state (:node opened) key)))\n     (let [handle (store/open (store/checked-spec spec))]\n       {:index-store handle\n        :node nil\n        :recovery (:recovery handle)\n        :publication-policy (:publication-policy handle)\n        :retain-index-on-reset? (store/retain-on-reset? handle)\n        :engine-inputs nil\n        :session nil}))))\n\n\n(defn durable?\n  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store the engine's own\n   selection opened (yin.repl.store/durable?).\"\n  [store]\n  (store/durable? store))\n\n\n(defn retain-on-reset?\n  \"True when a session rebuild continues `store`'s published index rather\n   than starting an empty one: the store's declared policy, or the\n   durable directory's own fact when it declares none\n   (yin.repl.store/retain-on-reset?).\"\n  [store]\n  (store/retain-on-reset? store))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"Release `store`'s lifecycle resources.  Idempotent, and the one place a\n   composition's resource owner closes the store it opened\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  [store]\n  (store/close! store))\n   through.  A custody composition (:custody, yin.vm.ucf.compose) rides the\n   shell as data; the step owner below is the only thing that steps it.\n\n   `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage composition\n   past the engine's own two stores.  When it names the parsed\n   `:index-store-spec` as one of its own (`:composition-spec?`), `:open`\n   opens it and answers the two values of the ownership split: `:index-store`,\n   the generic `dao.jing` handle the engine is constructed with, and\n   `:session`, the transport state the composition keeps and steps beside\n   the engine — never inside it.  What the engine additionally needs to\n   drive that store arrives as `:engine-inputs` of the same answer (a\n   prepared `:link-source`, the composition's `:host-modules`), so a\n   `(reset)` or a `(vm ...)` rebuild reconstructs a session that still\n   resolves signed names and still serves the composition's modules.\n\n   The engine value lands at `:repl`, where the driver and the endpoint\n   read it, and the composition's transport state at `:session`; there is\n   no third place a node could hide.  A construction that fails after the\n   store was opened releases what it acquired (`release-store!`) and\n   answers its own refusal.\n\n   `:admission` is the session's admission policy, by default `{}`: the\n   publisher key's own principal only.  It is apart from `:principals`: a\n   declared publisher is not a trusted one.\"\n  ([opts] (boot opts nil))\n  ([opts composition]\n   (let [spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n         open (:open composition)\n         composition-spec? (:composition-spec? composition)\n         comp-store (when (and open composition-spec?\n                               (composition-spec? spec))\n                      (open spec opts))\n         repl-inputs (cond-> (if comp-store\n                               (merge {:index-store (:index-store comp-store)\n                                       :recovery (:recovery comp-store)\n                                       :publication-policy\n                                       (:publication-policy comp-store)}\n                                      (:engine-inputs comp-store))\n                               {:index-store-spec spec})\n                       true (assoc :publisher-key (:publisher-key opts)\n                                   :principals (:principals opts)\n                                   :admission (:admission opts {})\n                                   :custody (:custody opts))\n                       (:vm-type opts) (assoc :vm-type (:vm-type opts)))\n         state (try\n                 (driver/create-state\n                   {:host (or (:adapter opts) (host/websocket))\n                    :repl (repl.frontends/create-state repl-inputs)})\n                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                   (when comp-store (release-store! composition comp-store))\n                   (throw e)))]\n     (cond-> (assoc state :composition composition :swap-store swap-store)\n       (:session comp-store) (assoc :session (:session comp-store))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n                            (some-> (or home (home-dir*))\n                                    (str \"/.yin/\" node-name))))\n             saved (when (and node-dir (not reset?))\n                     (state/load-flags node-dir table))\n             {:keys [flags rest]} (state/split-args args table)\n             resolved (state/resolve-flags saved flags unset)\n             args (into (state/flags->args resolved table) rest)\n             made (when (and new-key (:ensure-key! composition))\n                    ((:ensure-key! composition) new-key))\n             opts (cond-> (try (parse-args args composition)\n                               (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                         :clj Throwable\n                                         :cljs :default)\n                                      e\n                                 (throw (if (and saved (ex-data e))\n                                          (ex-info (str (ex-message e)\n                                                        \" (with the saved state in \"\n                                                        (state/path node-dir)\n                                                        \"; --reset forgets it)\")\n                                                   (ex-data e))\n                                          e))))\n                    made (assoc :startup-lines made)\n                    adapter (assoc :adapter adapter))]\n         (if-some [path (:keygen opts)]\n           ((:keygen! composition) path)\n           (let [key (when-some [path (:publisher-key-file opts)]\n                       ((:load-key composition) path))\n                 opts (cond-> opts key (assoc :publisher-key key))\n                 state' (boot (assoc opts\n                                     :ws-host (or (:adapter opts)\n                                                  (host/websocket)))\n                              composition)\n                 server (boot-server opts)\n                 lines (into (composition-startup-lines state')\n                             (when node-dir\n                               (save-state! node-dir saved resolved reset?\n                                            table)))]\n             {:opts (cond-> opts\n                      (seq lines) (update :startup-lines\n                                          #(into (vec %) lines)))\n              :state state'\n              :server server}))))\n     (catch #?(:cljd Object\n               :clj Throwable\n               :cljs :default)\n            e\n       (if (ex-data e)\n         {:refusal (or (ex-message e) (str e))}\n         (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  \"Print why the composition refused to start and end the process with a\n   failing status, so a refused startup never looks like a working shell.\"\n  [refusal]\n  (println refusal)\n  #?(:cljd (io/exit 1)\n     :jolt (do (flush) (System/exit 1))\n     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 1)\n     :cljs (.exit js/process 1)))\n\n\n(defn- custody-of\n  [state]\n  (get-in state [:repl :custody]))\n  \"The node composed from checked `opts` over the opened `local` store.\"\n  [opts local]\n  (let [{:keys [peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes bind!]}\n        opts\n        [requests answers facts ticks traffic ledger] (repeatedly 6 ring)\n        socket? (boolean (seq peers))\n        ;; The effective transport configuration, resolved once here and\n        ;; used consistently by every consumer of it: the DHT state, the\n        ;; store front's own oversize refusal, and the payload capability\n        ;; a storage composition declares (`payload-budget`).  Three\n        ;; consumers reading three defaults is how a bound and a budget\n        ;; come to disagree.\n        message-bound (or (::dht/max-message-bytes opts)\n                          (::dht/max-message-bytes dht/defaults))\n        composition (cond-> {:local local\n                             :requests requests\n                             :answers answers\n                             :facts facts\n                             :ticks ticks\n                             ::dht/id (dht/bytes->hex\n                                        (secure-random-bytes dht/id-length))\n                             ::dht/publish? publish?\n                             ::dht/bootstrap (vec peers)\n                             ::dht/bind-host bind-host}\n                      socket? (assoc :traffic traffic\n                                     ::dht/secret (secure-random-bytes\n                                                    secret-length)\n                                     ::dht/max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes))\n        seam (when socket?\n               (bind! {:identity (str \"dao.space.dht:\"\n                                      (subs (::dht/id composition) 0 16))\n                       :deposit traffic\n                       :bind-host bind-host\n                       :bind-port bind-port\n                       :max-bytes (::dht/max-datagram dht/defaults)}))\n        ;; the DHT handle's put checks (address, oversize) over :local; its\n        ;; own replicate request goes to a sink, since the node's step\n        ;; owns every request (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.5)\n        front (dht/store-handle\n                {:local local\n                 :requests (ring 1)\n                 :max-message-bytes message-bound})\n        closed? (volatile! false)]\n    {:peers (vec peers)\n     :publish? publish?\n     :message-bound message-bound\n     :limits (select-keys opts [:max-backlog :repair-batch :max-open\n                                :repair-slots :repair-ticks :repair-max-ticks\n                                :max-repairing])\n     :composition composition\n     :dht (when-not socket? (dht/state composition))\n     :seam seam\n     :traffic-cursor (when socket? (oldest traffic))\n     :facts (oldest facts)\n     :ledger ledger\n     :ledger-cursor (oldest ledger)\n     :origin nil\n     :reading nil\n     :window (new-ledger)\n     :window-lost? false\n     :pubs []\n                                 (finally\n                                   (jing/close! local)))))}}))\n\n\n(defn join\n  \"Join the DHT from `opts` and answer the node:\n\n   * `:local`: the node's own `dao.jing` store, already opened (and, if\n     it is a directory, already locked) by the caller, as `yin.repl` does;\n     or `:dir`, a directory `join` opens as the durable directory store\n     (`dao.space.store/open`): exclusively, under the directory lock, so\n     a second owner in this process or another is refused naming it, and\n     the lock is held until `close!`;\n   * `:peers`: bootstrap contacts `[{:host ip :port p} ...]`, none for\n     solo;\n   * `:publish?`: whether everything in the local store is public;\n   * `:bind-host`, `:bind-port`: the socket's address, loopback and\n     ephemeral by default;\n   * `:max-inbound-bytes`: the inbound storage bound;\n   * `:bind!`: the datagram host seam, `default-bind` by default;\n   * `:max-backlog`, `:repair-batch`, `:max-open`, `:repair-slots`,\n     `:repair-ticks`, `:repair-max-ticks`, `:max-repairing`: the\n     backlog and repair bounds (`defaults`).\n\n   Refuses an invalid option with its reason.  The node owns `:local`\n   from here: `close!` closes it.\"\n  [opts]\n  (let [opts (merge defaults {:bind! (default-bind)} opts)]\n    (when-some [why (option-refusal opts)]\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.space.dht/join: \" why)\n                      (dissoc opts :bind! :local))))\n    (let [local (local-store opts)]\n      (try\n        (node-over opts local)\n        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n          ;; a directory join opened: release it, lock included\n          (when-not (:local opts) (jing/close! local))\n          (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn store\n  \"The node's `dao.jing` byte-store handle: put inserts into the local\n   store and records the address for the node's next publication,\n   answering the local verdict at once; get reads the local store; close\n   closes the socket and the local store.\"\n  [node]\n  (:handle node))\n\n\n(defn local\n  \"The node's own local `dao.jing` store.\"\n  [node]\n  (get-in node [:composition :local]))\n\n\n(defn message-bound\n  \"The effective transport message bound `node` composes under: the most\n   encoded bytes one DHT message carries.  Resolved once, at `join`, and\n   the same number the store front's oversize refusal uses, so a caller\n   that sizes anything against the transport reads the transport's own\n   answer instead of a default it guessed\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 5).\"\n  [node]\n  (:message-bound node))\n\n\n(defn payload-budget\n  \"The payload capability `node`'s transport declares: the most payload\n   bytes one `:store` message can carry inside `message-bound`, derived by\n   the transport's own encoder and envelope (`dao.jing.dht/payload-budget`)\n   and never hardcoded.\n\n   This is the number a storage composition over this node declares as its\n31:(defn parse-trust\n49:(def file-name \"state.edn\")\n52:(def version 1)\n55:(def ^:private engine-saved-flags\n60:   [\"--vm\" :value]\n61:   [\"--port\" :value]\n62:   [\"--codec\" :value]\n63:   [\"--headless\" :switch]])\n66:(def ^:private engine-kinds (into {} engine-saved-flags))\n69:(def ^:private engine-one-shot-flags\n74:(defn flag-table\n101:(defn- value-of\n111:(defn split-args\n145:(defn flags->args\n159:(defn resolve-flags\n167:(defn changed\n177:(defn describe\n191:(defn- config-key\n196:(defn- refuse\n202:(defn- text->config\n248:(defn path\n254:(defn- read-text\n302:(defn load-flags\n320:(defn- mkdirs!\n327:(defn- render\n340:(defn save!\n      flush-out))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Section 5.1: the byte-store handle\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn store-handle\n  \"The plain-data dao.jing byte-store handle over a DHT composition's\n   :local and :requests: put-bytes-fn validates, refuses an oversize store\n   message, inserts into :local, appends {:dao.jing.dht/replicate address}\n   and returns the local verdict at once -- never the acknowledgement,\n   which is the :dao.jing.dht/sent fact. get-bytes-fn reads :local only\n   and never touches the network; close-fn closes :local.\"\n  [{:keys [local requests max-message-bytes]}]\n  (when-not (and (ifn? (:put-bytes-fn local)) (ifn? (:get-bytes-fn local)))\n    (throw (defect \"store-handle needs a :local byte-store handle\"\n             {:local local})))\n  (when-not (and requests (stream/writer? requests))\n    (throw (defect \"store-handle needs a :requests writer\" {})))\n  (let [limit (or max-message-bytes (::max-message-bytes defaults))]\n    {:local local\n     :requests requests\n     :put-bytes-fn\n     (fn [address bs]\n       (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n         (throw (defect \"content address does not match the bytes\"\n                  {:address address})))\n       (when (oversize? limit address bs)\n         (throw (defect \"the store message exceeds max-message-bytes\"\n                  {:address address, :reason ::oversize,\n                   :max-message-bytes limit})))\n       (let [verdict ((:put-bytes-fn local) address bs)]\n         (stream/append! requests {::replicate address})\n         verdict))\n     :get-bytes-fn (fn [address not-found]\n                     ((:get-bytes-fn local) address not-found))\n     :close-fn (fn [] (jing/close! local))}))\n19: * (EINVAL), never truncated at it. Path bytes are copied into a terminated\n33: * record lock (fcntl F_SETLK, F_WRLCK, SEEK_SET, 0, 0; release is close, so\n34: * there is no unlock entry), realpath (the C-owned result copied out and\n35: * freed before return), rename, a directory open+fsync+close, an O_EXCL\n37: * non-blocking read-only open, and classify/fclassify (lstat/stat/fstat kept\n209:/* ftruncate to len: 0 or -errno. */\n210:JOLT_FILE_EXPORT int64_t jolt_file_truncate(int64_t fd, int64_t len) {\n215:    r = ftruncate((int)fd, (off_t)len);\n220:/* A full fsync (not fdatasync, not a port flush): 0 or -errno. Not retried:\n221:   after a failed fsync the kernel may have dropped the dirty pages, so a\n223:JOLT_FILE_EXPORT int64_t jolt_file_sync(int64_t fd) {\n225:  return fsync((int)fd) == 0 ? 0 : -errno;\n317:/* What an open descriptor is (fstat): the recheck after a non-blocking open. */\n373: * Non-blocking so a FIFO swapped in after classify cannot block the open;\n376:JOLT_FILE_EXPORT int64_t jolt_file_open_read(const uint8_t *path, int64_t n) {\n381: * The whole-file write lock: fcntl(F_SETLK) with F_WRLCK, SEEK_SET, start 0,\n382: * length 0, the same record-lock family as the JVM's FileChannel.tryLock and\n383: * Dart's lockSync, so the three exclude one another. Non-blocking (no\n386: * locks are per process and drop when any descriptor on the inode closes).\n388:JOLT_FILE_EXPORT int64_t jolt_file_lock(int64_t fd) {\n390:  struct flock fl;\n447: * O_CLOEXEC), fsync, close. 0, or the -errno of the first step that failed\n448: * (an fsync failure is reported even though the close then succeeds).\n450:JOLT_FILE_EXPORT int64_t jolt_file_sync_dir(const uint8_t *path, int64_t n) {\n453:  int err = fsync((int)fd) == 0 ? 0 : errno;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
