{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '(posix-file|posix\\\\.file)/(realpath|lock-file\"'!|fidentity|write-new-private!|classify|open)'\"' src test | head -100; sed -n '40,100p' src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc; sed -n '345,360p;380,445p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '80,98p' src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc; tail -20 /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2/build/p2/static-matrix.log; ls -lh /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2/build/p2\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:186:     :jolt (posix-file/realpath dir)\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:222:     :jolt (let [h (posix-file/lock-file! path)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc:166:  #?(:jolt (posix-file/open path)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc:276:     :jolt (when-not (= :absent (posix-file/classify path false))\nsrc/cljc/yin/shell/cli.cljc:186:       :jolt (when (= :exists (posix-file/write-new-private! path (text/utf8-encode text)))\n   subcommands, the key file, the help and the banner text.  The rest is the\n   store and its transport lifecycle, each entry one function value taken\n   statically from the namespace that owns it, so the wiring is identical on\n   the JVM, on Node and on Dart and no host resolves a symbol at runtime\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 6 and 7).\n\n   The lifecycle functions all take the one composition session\n   `{:engine … :node … :key …}` and are driven by the engine driver's single\n   tick: `:step` advances the transport and answers its lines and its own\n   events, `:recheck-on-tick` serves the link and call media the engine\n   parks on and translates those events before they cross inward, and\n   `:stop!`/`:stopped?`/`:close!` are the one resource owner's exit — asked\n   once, completed by `:step`, and forced only by the drain's last resort.\"\n  (merge (cli/hooks)\n         {:composition-spec? shell.store/composition-spec?\n          :open shell.store/open\n          :close-store! shell.store/close!\n          :step shell.dht/step\n          :recheck-on-tick shell.session/recheck-on-tick\n          :recheck-after-input shell.session/recheck-after-input\n          :stop! shell.dht/stop!\n          :stopped? shell.dht/stopped?\n          :close! shell.dht/close!\n          :busy? shell.dht/busy?\n          :refusal shell.dht/refusal\n          :admitting? shell.dht/admitting?\n          :startup-lines shell.dht/follow-lines}))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :jolt nil\n   :clj\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped JVM entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:jolt\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped jolt entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:cljs\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped Node entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:cljd\n   (do\n     (defn -main\n       \"The shipped Dart entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n       [& args]\n       (repl.main/main! args composition))\n\n     (defn ^{:dart/name main} run-main\n       [args]\n\n(defn- composition-step\n  \"One transport step of the composition this host carries, at the host's\n   clock reading: `[state lines events]`, the events in the composition's\n   own vocabulary.  A host with no composition answers itself unchanged and\n   no events, so the engine's own tick path is the one that runs.\"\n  [state now]\n  (if-some [step (:step (:composition state))]\n    (if-some [session (session-of state)]\n      (let [[session' lines events] (step session now)]\n        [(with-session state session') lines events])\n      [state [] []])\n    [state [] []]))\n\n\n(defn- composition-recheck\n\n(defn- composition-stop\n  \"Ask the composition's transport state to stop, once: its board server,\n   its dials and its socket are asked here and completed by `step`, and a\n   host never reaches past the composition to any of them.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [stop! (:stop! (:composition state))]\n    (if-some [session (session-of state)]\n      (with-session state (stop! session))\n      state)\n    state))\n\n\n(defn- composition-stopped?\n  \"True when the composition owes nothing at exit — no transport state, or\n   transport state whose own exit condition is met.  A host with no\n   composition owes nothing.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [stopped? (:stopped? (:composition state))]\n    (boolean (stopped? (session-of state)))\n    true))\n\n\n(defn- composition-refusal\n  \"The text that refused the composition's store after startup (a socket\n   that could not bind, a hydration that could not complete), or nil.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [refusal (:refusal (:composition state))]\n    (refusal (session-of state))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-admitting?\n  \"Whether the shell may evaluate: a composition with a hydration still\n   outstanding, or one whose hydration was refused, admits nothing, and\n   every typed line waits in the input medium.  A host with no composition\n   always admits.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [admitting? (:admitting? (:composition state))]\n    (boolean (admitting? (session-of state)))\n    true))\n\n\n(defn- composition-busy?\n  \"True while the composition owes the shell a line, which keeps the tick\n   owner at its base cadence.\"\n  [state]\n  (boolean (when-some [busy? (:busy? (:composition state))]\n             (busy? (session-of state)))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-close!\n  \"The bounded drain's last resort: whatever the composition still owes\n   after `stop!` and its budget of `step`s is asked for once more and not\n   awaited.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [close! (:close! (:composition state))]\n    (close! (session-of state))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-startup-lines\n  \"What the composition states at startup about the session it opened —\n   where it follows a published head, and whether one is installed yet —\n   or nothing for a host that carries no composition.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [lines (:startup-lines (:composition state))]\n    (vec (lines (session-of state)))\n   kind] ...] :one-shot-flags #{flag ...}}`; its flags are appended to the\n   engine's, so a composition's flags are saved and resumed beside them\n   and a run of the engine alone is unchanged.  A flag named in both keeps\n   the engine's kind.\n\n   The no-argument table is the engine's own and nothing else.  This\n   namespace resolves no composition — not by require, not by symbol — so\n   the table it answers cannot vary with what else a build happens to\n   carry, and a composition hands its table in (yin.repl.main/startup's\n   `:flag-table`, yin.shell.cli/flag-table) instead of being discovered\n   from here.\"\n  ([] (flag-table nil))\n  ([{:keys [saved-flags one-shot-flags]}]\n   (let [saved (into engine-saved-flags\n                     (remove #(contains? engine-kinds (first %)))\n                     saved-flags)]\n     {:saved-flags saved\n      :kinds (into {} saved)\n      :one-shot-flags (into engine-one-shot-flags one-shot-flags)})))\nbash: /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2/.cache/local/chezscheme-10.4.1/bin/scheme: No such file or directory\ndiff: /var/folders/n0/xl3_1xkn0yd5trpq843l81840000gn/T/tmp.Q3a6OFRFYn/records-gambit.ss: No such file or directory\ngambitgencheck: host/gambit/records-gambit.ss is STALE — run 'make gambitgen'\ndiff: /var/folders/n0/xl3_1xkn0yd5trpq843l81840000gn/T/tmp.Q3a6OFRFYn/records-gambit.ss: No such file or directory\nmake: *** [gambitgencheck] Error 1\ntotal 8\n-rw-r--r--@  1 sto  staff     0B Nov 26 18:24 boot.log\n-rw-r--r--@  1 sto  staff     0B Nov 26 18:24 boot.path\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 57 sto  staff   1.8K Nov 26 18:24 datomworld\n-rw-r--r--@  1 sto  staff   453B Nov 26 18:24 static-matrix.log\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 sto  staff    64B Nov 26 18:25 tmp\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
