{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'submodules|\"'^LOCAL-ROOT'\"' Makefile | head -28; sed -n '45,68p' host/gambit/host-statics.ss; grep -E 'HEAD|make|bin/jolt' /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1f/build/p1f/matrix-verified.log | head -21; sed -n '1,42p' bin/jolt; ls -l /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1f/.cache/local/bin; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"140:deps: submodules $(JOLT-CHEZ)\n148:submodules:\n180:CI-GATES := submodules values recordinline corpus nsaudit unit documented grenadine clishim mvnhttp readscaling gcpolicy stacklimit footprint lazyretain compilescaling applyscaling lazyscaling vecscaling pipescaling chunkscaling printscaling complexity ioscaling hotscaling fastpathratio stdlibratio depssmoke taskssmoke scriptsmoke exitwait completionssmoke depscpcache depsunit \\\n190:TEST-GATES := submodules selfhost ci\n1248:tracecompilecost: submodules\n2268:devboot: submodules\n2277:gateboot: submodules\n                            (begin (set! miss2 miss1) (set! miss1 (cons t #f))))\n                        a)))))))))\n(define-syntax define-jhost-tag-pred\n  (syntax-rules ()\n    ((_ (name t) body ...) (define name (jhost-tag-memo (lambda (t) body ...))))))\n\n;; ---- registries ---------------------------------------------------------------\n;; class-ctors-tbl / register-class-ctor! are rt-core.ss's (a deftype registers\n;; its ctor there under its tag); class-statics-tbl / register-class-statics!\n;; are prelude-shims.ss's (compile-eval.ss registers the Compiler statics into\n;; it at load). The method registry is this file's.\n(define host-methods-tbl (make-hashtable string-hash string=?))   ; tag -> (method-ht)\n(define (register-host-methods! tag members)\n  (let ((h (or (hashtable-ref host-methods-tbl tag #f)\n               (let ((h (make-hashtable string-hash string=?)))\n                 (hashtable-set! host-methods-tbl tag h) h))))\n    (for-each (lambda (p) (hashtable-set! h (car p) (cdr p))) members)))\n;; The member NAME resolves to on TAG, or #f. There is no parent chain here:\n;; every jhost tag this target builds registers its own members.\n(define (host-method-ref tag name)\n  (let ((h (hashtable-ref host-methods-tbl tag #f)))\n    (and h (hashtable-ref h name #f))))\n;; A class token may arrive fully qualified (java.io.StringReader) or short\n;; (StringReader): exact first, then by last dotted segment.\nhost/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh: OK\nhost/gambit/ffi/make-digests.sh: OK\n  ok     make-hashtable (hash+equiv dropped, equal? test)\n== hasheq known answers (captured from the Chez build via bin/jolt) ==\n  ok     sa-make-boot-file -> native compilation is unsupported on the gambit target\n== rendering: jolt-pr-readable (captures from bin/jolt on Chez) ==\n#!/bin/sh\n# jolt — the pure-Chez jolt runtime. NO Janet.\n#\n# Compiles and evaluates jolt (Clojure) on Chez using the checked-in bootstrap\n# seed (host/chez/seed/). With only Chez installed it runs jolt end to end:\n#\n#   jolt -e \"(+ 1 2)\"             evaluate an expression\n#   jolt run -m app.core [args]   resolve deps.edn, run a namespace's -main\n#   jolt -M:alias [args]          run an alias's :main-opts\n#   jolt repl | path | <task>     REPL, print roots, or a deps.edn task\n#\n# The launcher cd's to the jolt repo root so the runtime's relative loads work;\n# the user's original cwd (the project dir, where deps.edn lives) is passed in\n# JOLT_PWD.\n#\n# $0 may be a SYMLINK. That is the natural way to put a checkout's jolt on PATH,\n# and it is what `#!/usr/bin/env jolt` executes, so follow the chain to the real\n# file before deriving the root from it: without this the root came out as the\n# symlink's own directory and the launcher died there looking for tools/version.sh\n# and host/chez/cli.ss. Hand-rolled rather than `readlink -f`, which is neither\n# POSIX nor present on older macOS.\ntarget=\"$0\"\nwhile [ -L \"$target\" ]; do\n  link=\"$(readlink \"$target\")\"\n  case \"$link\" in\n    /*) target=\"$link\" ;;\n    *)  target=\"$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$target\")\" && pwd)/$link\" ;;\n  esac\ndone\nroot=\"$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$target\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nexport JOLT_PWD=\"${JOLT_PWD:-$PWD}\"\n# How jolt re-invokes itself (babashka.tasks/clojure in a task). An installed\n# jolt is on PATH and needs no help; this checkout is not.\nexport JOLT_EXE=\"${JOLT_EXE:-$root/bin/jolt}\"\n\n# Identify the Chez Scheme executable. $JOLT_CHEZ is authoritative and is how the\n# Makefile hands down the one it selected — the same interpreter that mints the\n# seed and compiles target/dev/flat.so. A direct bin/jolt invocation does not\n# inherit that export, so it takes the Chez make recorded next to the dev boot\n# cache (any other pick makes that cache unusable), then the one make\n# provisioned. A Chez on PATH is never used: jolt runs on a Chez carrying its\n# kernel patches, which make builds (`make deps`) or which is passed in.\ntotal 0\n M host/gambit/ffi/DIGESTS.txt\n M host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm\n M host/gambit/yin-repl-driver.ss\n M host/gambit/yin/dao/posix/file.jolt\n?? host/gambit/yin/file.ss\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
