{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '96,176p' src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md; rg -n 'restart|resum|durable|replicat' test/*/yin/repl* test/*/yin/shell* | head -80; sed -n '1,110p' src/dev/gambit_ffi_cache.clj; cat /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p1f/build/p1f/acceptance-boot.log | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"### Durable Local Store\nTo persist definitions and evaluated code across restarts, pass a `file:` directory store:\n\n```bash\nclj -M:clj-yin-repl --index-store file:/tmp/my-repl-store\n```\n\n### Client / Server over WebSockets\nStart a headless or interactive server listening on a WebSocket port:\n\n```bash\nclj -M:clj-yin-repl --port 8080 --headless\n```\n\nFrom another REPL prompt, attach to the running server:\n\n```clojure\nyin> (connect \"daostream:ws://localhost:8080/repl\")\nAttaching to daostream:ws://localhost:8080/repl\nConnected to daostream:ws://localhost:8080/repl\n```\n\n- An absent URL path defaults to `/repl`; an explicit `/` remains `/`.\n- The wire codec defaults to CBOR. Use `--codec <cbor|transit>` on the server, and `(connect url :codec :transit)` or `:cbor` at the prompt. Both ends must match.\n- `--port` listens on all interfaces (`localhost` and the machine's IP) with **no authentication**—run it only on a trusted network. There is no `--host` flag.\n\n### Other Hosts (Node & Dart)\n`(host)` prints the runtime the shell runs on (`Host: JVM 21.0.5`, `Host: Node v25.6.1`, `Host: Dart`).\n\n- **ClojureScript (`cljs` on Node):**\n  ```bash\n  clj -M:cljs-yin-repl --port 8080 --headless\n  # Or compile to a standalone Node script:\n  npx shadow-cljs release yin-repl\n  node target/yin-repl.js --port 8080 --headless\n  ```\n\n- **ClojureDart (`cljd`):**\n  ```bash\n  clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build compile\n  dart run bin/yin_repl_main.dart --port 8080 --headless\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Working at the Prompt\n\n### Switching Language Frontends\nThe REPL ships with three frontends on every host: `:yang/clojure` (default), `:yang/php`, and `:yang/python` (ANTLR multi-target parser, revision f4). Switch languages using `(lang <id>)` with a qualified keyword:\n\n```clojure\nyin> (lang :yang/python)\n\"Switched to :yang/python\"\nyin> print(\"hello\")\nhello\n```\n\n- Selection requires a qualified id (`(lang :yang/python)` or `[id revision]`). Unqualified keywords like `(lang :python)` return `Error: unavailable-parser: ...`.\n- The Python frontend displays printed output followed by the value of the last top-level bare expression statement (rendered as Python `repr`; assignments or `None` display nothing). Frontend state is preserved across submissions and cleared on `(reset)` or `(vm ...)`.\n  - *Known edges:* Bare expressions inside compound statements (`if`/`for`) do not display; values captured before a later statement raises print after the error text; string `repr` escapes only code units `< 32` and `127`.\n\n### Switching Evaluator VMs\n`(vm :type)` selects one of four evaluators:\n- `:semantic` (default) — linear semantic VM\n- `:ast-walker` — tree walker\n- `:stack` — de Bruijn stack kernel\n- `:register` — de Bruijn register kernel\n\nSwitching rebuilds the session and clears value history.\n\n### Switching Index Stores: `(use-store ...)`\nAt a quiesced local `yin>` prompt, `(use-store <target> & <opts>)` switches the session's active `dao.jing` code-index store without restarting the REPL process:\n\n```clojure\n;; Engine-native targets:\nyin> (use-store \"mem\")                     ; or (use-store :mem)\nSwitched index store to mem (code index cleared)\n\nyin> (use-store \"file:/tmp/my-repl-store\")\nSwitched index store to file:/tmp/my-repl-store (empty code index)\n\nzsh:1: no matches found: test/*/yin/shell*\n(ns gambit-ffi-cache\n  \"Build and verify the worktree-local FFI artifacts independently of Yin's boot.\"\n  (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\n            [babashka.process :as p]\n            [build-cache :as cache]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]))\n\n\n(def ^:private ffi-dir \"host/gambit/ffi\")\n(def ^:private artifact-dir \"build/gambit-ffi\")\n(def ^:private bridge \"joltffi-bridge.o1\")\n\n\n(def ^:private artifacts\n  [bridge \"libjoltffi-fixture.dylib\" \"libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib\"\n   \"libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\"])\n\n\n(defn- with-lock\n  [dir f]\n  (cache/local-path! dir)\n  (fs/create-dirs dir)\n  (with-open [file (java.io.RandomAccessFile. (fs/file dir \".ffi.lock\") \"rw\")\n              channel (.getChannel file)\n              lock (.lock channel)]\n    (f)))\n\n\n(defn- hashes\n  [dir]\n  (into (sorted-map)\n        (for [name artifacts\n              :let [file (fs/path dir name)]\n              :when (fs/regular-file? file)]\n          [name (cache/file-digest file)])))\n\n\n(defn- read-stamp\n  [entry]\n  (let [stamp (fs/path entry \"artifacts.edn\")]\n    (when (fs/regular-file? stamp)\n      (try (edn/read-string (slurp (str stamp)))\n           (catch Exception _ nil)))))\n\n\n(defn- key-for\n  [jolt-home prefix]\n  (let [ffi (fs/path jolt-home ffi-dir)\n        toolchain [\"bin/gsi\" \"bin/gsc\" \"bin/gambuild-C\" \"include/gambit.h\"\n                   \"lib/libgambit.a\" \"lib/libgambitgsi.a\" \"lib/libgambitgsc.a\"]]\n    (cache/digest\n      {:recipe (cache/file-digest \"src/dev/gambit_ffi_cache.clj\")\n       :platform [(System/getProperty \"os.name\") (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n       :c-compilers (mapv #(cache/checked-output % \"--version\") (keep fs/which [\"cc\" \"gcc\"]))\n       :compiler-flags (mapv #(System/getenv %) [\"CORCXXFLAGS_GAMBUILD\" \"LDFLAGS_GAMBUILD\"])\n       :ffi (into (sorted-map)\n                  (map (fn [[path digest]] [(str (fs/relativize ffi path)) digest]))\n                  (cache/snapshot [ffi]))\n       :gambit (mapv #(cache/file-digest (fs/path prefix %)) toolchain)})))\n\n\n(defn- stage!\n  [opts watchdog message & command]\n  (.println System/err (str \"jolt-gambit: \" message \" [600 s watchdog]\"))\n  (apply p/shell (assoc opts :shutdown nil) \"sh\" (str watchdog) \"600\" command))\n\n\n(defn- build-bridge!\n  [stage jolt-home prefix]\n  (let [ffi (fs/path stage ffi-dir)\n        dir (fs/path stage artifact-dir)\n        opts {:dir dir}\n        watchdog (fs/path ffi \"watchdog.sh\")\n        gsc (str (fs/path prefix \"bin/gsc\"))\n        shared-flags (case (System/getProperty \"os.name\")\n                       \"Mac OS X\" [\"-dynamiclib\"]\n                       \"Linux\" [\"-shared\" \"-fPIC\"])\n        fixture! (fn [output input & libraries]\n                   (apply stage! opts watchdog (str \"Building \" output \" (usually seconds)\")\n                          \"cc\" \"-O1\" (concat shared-flags [\"-o\" output (str (fs/path ffi input))]\n                                             libraries)))]\n    (fs/create-dirs (fs/parent ffi))\n    (fs/copy-tree (fs/path jolt-home ffi-dir) ffi)\n    (fs/create-dirs dir)\n    (.println System/err \"jolt-gambit: Verifying pinned FFI sources and toolchain\")\n    (doseq [script [\"record-toolchain.sh\" \"verify-digests.sh\"]]\n      (p/shell {:dir stage :shutdown nil} \"sh\" (str (fs/path ffi script)) prefix))\n    (doseq [source [\"joltffi-bridge.scm\" \"generated-shims.scm\"]]\n      (fs/copy (fs/path ffi source) (fs/path dir source)))\n    ;; Gambit looks up a dynamic module by its .o1 name. Carry that name\n    ;; into the generated C before compiling and linking under separate deadlines.\n    (stage! opts watchdog \"Translating the FFI bridge from Scheme to C (can take minutes)\"\n            gsc \"-c\" \"-module-ref\" bridge \"joltffi-bridge.scm\")\n    (stage! opts watchdog \"Compiling the FFI bridge C object (can take minutes)\"\n            gsc \"-obj\" \"-cc-options\" \"-D___DYNAMIC\" \"joltffi-bridge.c\")\n    (stage! (assoc opts :extra-env {\"GAMBITDIR_INCLUDE\" (str (fs/path prefix \"include\"))\n                                    \"GAMBITDIR_LIB\" (str (fs/path prefix \"lib\"))\n                                    \"BUILD_DYN_INPUT_FILENAMES_PARAM\" \"joltffi-bridge.o\"\n                                    \"BUILD_DYN_OUTPUT_FILENAME_PARAM\" bridge})\n            watchdog \"Linking the FFI bridge module (usually seconds)\"\n            (str (fs/path prefix \"bin/gambuild-C\")) \"dyn\")\n    (fixture! \"libjoltffi-fixture.dylib\" \"joltffi-fixture.c\")\n    (fixture! \"libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib\" \"joltffi-fixture2.c\")\n    (fixture! \"libjoltffi-dep.dylib\" \"joltffi-dep.c\")\n    (fixture! \"libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\" \"joltffi-unloadable.c\" \"libjoltffi-dep.dylib\")\n    dir))\n\n\n(defn ensure!\n  \"Return a verified bridge cache entry built from the pinned FFI inputs.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
