{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1268,1390p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '1,110p' host/gambit/source-loader.ss; tail -4 build/p2/shared-component.err; tail -6 build/p2/first.err\"","aggregated_output":"     (defn -main\n       \"The engine's own JVM entry point: the `mem` and `file:<dir>` stores\n        and no storage composition.  The shipped product entry point is\n        `yin.shell.main/-main`, which supplies one.\"\n       [& args]\n       (main! args nil))))\n\n\n#?(:jolt\n   (do\n     (defn main!\n       \"One plain-thread owner. Stdin deposits only; EOF deposits (quit).\n        One host WebSocket instance serves the shell, a storage\n        composition's own endpoints and --port; every owner round polls its\n        sockets (headless included) and the instance is closed before exit,\n        however the drain ended.  Saved flags persist in the node\n        directory, as on the JVM (J4d): --reset forgets them and --no-state\n        neither reads nor writes them.\n\n        `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage\n        composition, nil for a host that carries none.\"\n       [args composition]\n       (let [adapter (host/websocket)\n             started (startup args {:persist? true :adapter adapter\n                                    :composition composition})]\n         (when (contains? started :exit) (exit-with! started))\n         (if-some [refusal (:refusal started)]\n           (refuse! refusal)\n           (let [{:keys [opts state server]} started\n                 headless? (boolean (:headless? opts))\n                 eof? (atom false)\n                 w (wake/make-wake)\n                 line! (fn [line]\n                         (if (nil? line)\n                           (do (reset! eof? true)\n                               (driver/submit-line! (:input state) \"(quit)\"))\n                           (driver/submit-line! (:input state) line)))\n                 sleep! (fn [ms]\n                          (wake/sleep-fds! w ms (:pump adapter)\n                                           (when-not (or headless? @eof?) line!)))]\n             (doseq [line (banner opts composition)] (println line))\n             (when-not headless? (print prompt))\n             (flush)\n             ;; the exit status leaves through System/exit, which skips the\n             ;; finally, so the exit path closes the instance itself too\n             (try\n               (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n                           sleep! (fn [status]\n                                    ((:close-host! adapter))\n                                    (wake/close! w)\n                                    (flush)\n                                    (System/exit status)))\n               (finally\n                 ((:close-host! adapter))\n                 (wake/close! w)))))))\n\n     (defn -main\n       \"The engine's own jolt entry point: the `mem` and `file:<dir>` stores\n        and no storage composition.  The shipped product entry point is\n        `yin.shell.main/-main`, which supplies one.\"\n       [& args]\n       (main! args nil))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; cljs (Node): a readline handler that only appends, and one interval owner\n;; =============================================================================\n\n#?(:cljs\n   (do\n     (defn run-node!\n       \"The tick owner on Node: one wake source arms exactly one timer per\n        round, at the interval `cadence-step` computes over\n        `default-cadence`.  Returns the wake so the composition can wire its\n        line producers (the readline handlers, the stop signals) as\n        `nudge!` callers.\n\n        `repl-step` is synchronous and the Node event loop is single\n        threaded, so a tick cannot overlap itself.  The box is host cadence\n        plumbing: the tick is the only reader and writer of it.  `:stopping`\n        is nil while the shell runs and a tick budget afterwards: the drain\n        is entered when there is an endpoint to stop, a head board that\n        still owes its stop-and-drain, or custody owes a control write\n        (`shutdown-enter?` -- a REPL without --port drains its owed custody\n        writes too), the head board and the endpoint are asked to stop\n        once, and the drain steps at the base interval until the endpoint\n        has stopped AND the board owes nothing AND custody owes nothing\n        (`shutdown-drained?`) or the budget ends.  `exit!`, the process\n        exit by default, is the seam a test injects to drive the owner to\n        its end.\"\n       ([state server rl] (run-node! state server rl #(js/process.exit %)))\n       ([state server rl exit!]\n        (let [box (atom {:state state :server server :stopping nil\n                         :cadence (cadence/init default-cadence)})\n              wake-ref (volatile! nil)\n              finish! (fn []\n                        (wake/disarm! @wake-ref)\n                        (when rl (.close rl))\n                        (close-index-store! (:state @box))\n                        (exit! (exit-status (:state @box))))\n              tick (fn []\n                     ;; The interval timer this namespace replaced fired\n                     ;; again whatever happened, so a tick whose body throws\n                     ;; must not kill the owner: arm the fallback first and\n                     ;; let the body's own `arm!` replace it. `finish!`\n                     ;; disarms, so a finished owner parks nothing.\n                     (wake/arm! @wake-ref tick-millis)\n                     (let [{:keys [state server stopping cadence]} @box]\n                       (if (nil? stopping)\n                         (let [[state' server' lines] (step-all state server\n                                                                (js/Date.now))]\n                           (reset! box {:state state'\n                                        :server server'\n                                        :stopping nil\n                                        :cadence cadence})\n                           (doseq [line lines]\n                             (js/console.log line))\n                           (cond\n                             (:running? state')\n                             (let [{:keys [cadence-state sleep-ms]}\n                                   (cadence/cadence-step\n                                     cadence (moved? state' server' lines))]\n                               (swap! box assoc :cadence cadence-state)\n;; Opt-in native source namespace loading for embedded applications. Unlike the\n;; Chez loader, this only interprets source. It has no cache, FASL, AOT, runtime\n;; dependency discovery, or native-library discovery.\n\n(define (gambit-namespace-path name)\n  (let ((chars (string->list name)))\n    (let check ((rest chars) (need-name? #t))\n      (unless (cond\n                ((null? rest) (not need-name?))\n                ((char=? (car rest) #\\.) (and (not need-name?) (check (cdr rest) #t)))\n                ((or (char-alphabetic? (car rest)) (char-numeric? (car rest))\n                     (memv (car rest) '(#\\- #\\_)))\n                 (check (cdr rest) #f))\n                (else #f))\n        (throw-jvm 'IllegalArgumentException (string-append \"Invalid namespace: \" name))))\n    (list->string\n      (map (lambda (ch) (case ch ((#\\.) #\\/) ((#\\-) #\\_) (else ch))) chars))))\n\n;; Gambit's reader tags bracket-delimited lists. Raw Scheme in loaded\n;; Jolt libraries uses R6RS brackets as grouping delimiters.\n(define (gambit-source-scheme-form datum)\n  (define (read-list items)\n    (if (pair? items)\n        (cons (gambit-source-scheme-form (car items)) (read-list (cdr items)))\n        items))\n  (cond\n    ((pair? datum)\n     (case (car datum)\n       ((|[...]|) (read-list (cdr datum)))\n       ((endianness)\n        (unless (and (list? datum) (= (length datum) 2)\n                     (memq (cadr datum) '(big little)))\n          (error \"invalid endianness\" datum))\n        (list 'quote (cadr datum)))\n       (else (read-list datum))))\n    ((vector? datum) (vector-map gambit-source-scheme-form datum))\n    (else datum)))\n\n(define (gambit-source-scheme-eval text)\n  (let ((port (open-input-string (jolt-need-string text))))\n    (input-port-readtable-set! port\n      (readtable-sharing-allowed?-set (input-port-readtable port) #f))\n    (let loop ((last jolt-nil))\n      (let ((form (read port)))\n        (if (eof-object? form)\n            last\n            (loop (eval (gambit-source-scheme-form form))))))))\n\n;; Each root is (directory suffix ...), in classpath order. BOOTED names denote\n;; whole namespaces supplied by the embedding host and take precedence over\n;; files. A mere intern or :as-alias never satisfies a source dependency.\n(define (gambit-install-source-loader! roots booted)\n  (define loaded (make-table test: string=?))\n  (define (find-file name)\n    (let ((base (gambit-namespace-path name)))\n      (let find-root ((rest roots))\n        (and (pair? rest)\n             (let find-suffix ((suffixes (cdar rest)))\n               (if (null? suffixes)\n                   (find-root (cdr rest))\n                   (let ((file (string-append (caar rest) \"/\" base (car suffixes))))\n                     (if (and (file-exists? file) (eq? 'regular (file-type file)))\n                         file\n                         (find-suffix (cdr suffixes))))))))))\n  (define (load-namespace name force?)\n    (when force?\n      (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n                 \"namespace reload is unsupported on the gambit source loader\"))\n    (unless (member name booted)\n      (case (table-ref loaded name #f)\n        ((ready) #f)\n        ((loading)\n         (throw-jvm 'IllegalStateException (string-append \"Cyclic namespace load: \" name)))\n        ((failed)\n         (throw-jvm 'IllegalStateException (string-append \"Earlier namespace load failed: \" name)))\n        (else\n         (let ((file (find-file name)))\n           (unless file\n             (throw-jvm 'FileNotFoundException (string-append \"No source for namespace: \" name)))\n           (table-set! loaded name 'loading)\n           (when (getenv \"JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE\" #f)\n             (fprintf (current-error-port) \"[~as] load ~a\\n\" (inexact->exact (round (time->seconds (current-time)))) name)\n             (force-output (current-error-port)))\n           (guard (e (#t (table-set! loaded name 'failed) (raise e)))\n             (jolt-with-ns-bound\n               (lambda ()\n                 (parameterize ((rdr-read-features (cons \"gambit\" (rdr-read-features))))\n                   (jolt-eval-string (call-with-input-file file gambit-read-all) file))\n                 (unless (string=? name (chez-current-ns))\n                   (throw-jvm 'IllegalStateException\n                              (string-append file \": expected namespace \" name)))))\n             (when (getenv \"JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE\" #f)\n               (fprintf (current-error-port) \"[~as] ready ~a\\n\" (inexact->exact (round (time->seconds (current-time)))) name)\n               (force-output (current-error-port)))\n             (table-set! loaded name 'ready)))))))\n  (set-ns-load-target! load-namespace)\n  (set-ns-with-load-opts!\n    (lambda (flags proceed)\n      (unless (null? flags)\n        (throw-jvm 'UnsupportedOperationException\n                   (string-append \"require option is unsupported on the gambit source loader: :\"\n                                  (car flags))))\n      (proceed #f)))\n  (def-var! \"jolt.host\" \"scheme-eval-string\" gambit-source-scheme-eval)\n  (def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"require\" jolt-require)\n  (def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"use\" jolt-use)\n  load-namespace)\n[1795692942s] load jolt.scheme\n[1795692944s] ready jolt.scheme\n[1795692944s] ready dao.host.hash\n[1795692944s] load dao.host.text\n[1795692886s] load yin.vm.debruijn\n[1795692929s] ready yin.vm.debruijn\n[1795692929s] load yin.vm.ucf\n[1795692929s] ready yin.vm.ucf\n[1795692931s] ready yin.vm.semantic.scan\n[1795692931s] load yin.vm.debruijn-code\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
