{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_88","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"set -e\npython3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\n\np = Path(\\\"host/gambit/yin/file.ss\\\")\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\\\"\\\"\\\"(let* ((path (gambit-yin-absolute-path path))\n         (kind (gambit-yin-file-kind path #f)))\n    (cond\n      ((eq? kind '\\\\''absent) (keyword #f \\\"absent\\\"))\n      ((or (eq? kind '\\\\''regular)\n           (and (eq? kind '\\\\''symbolic-link)\n                (eq? (gambit-yin-file-kind path #t) '\\\\''regular)))\\\"\\\"\\\",\n              \\\"\\\"\\\"(let* ((path (gambit-yin-absolute-path path))\n         (bounded? (not (jolt-nil? limit)))\n         (entry (gambit-yin-file-kind path (not bounded?))))\n    (cond\n      ((eq? entry '\\\\''absent) (keyword #f \\\"absent\\\"))\n      ((or (eq? entry '\\\\''regular)\n           (and (eq? entry '\\\\''symbolic-link)\n                (eq? (gambit-yin-file-kind path #t) '\\\\''regular)))\\\"\\\"\\\")\ns = s.replace(\\\"(if (jolt-nil? limit) size (min size (+ 1 (jnum->exact limit))))\\\",\n              \\\"(if bounded? (min size (+ 1 (jnum->exact limit))) size)\\\")\np.write_text(s)\n\np = Path(\\\"host/gambit/yin/dao/posix/file.jolt\\\")\ns = p.read_text().replace(\\\"(defn read-bounded [path limit] (read-file path limit))\\\",\n                         \\\"\\\"\\\"(defn read-bounded [path limit]\n  (when-not (and (integer? limit) (<= 0 limit 2147483646))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \\\"read-bounded limit out of range: \\\" limit)\n                    {:path path :limit limit})))\n  (read-file path limit))\\\"\\\"\\\")\np.write_text(s)\n\np = Path(\\\"host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt\\\")\ns = p.read_text().replace(\\\"\\\"\\\"         :help-lines (mapv (fn [line]\n                             (if (= line \\\"  --index-store s   mem (default), file:<dir> or dht:<dir>\\\")\n                               \\\"  --index-store s   mem (default), dht: (memory), file:<dir> or dht:<dir>\\\"\n                               line))\n                           (:help-lines shell/composition))))\\\"\\\"\\\",\n                         \\\"\\\"\\\"         :help-lines (into (:help-lines shell/composition)\n                           [\\\"\\\"\n                            \\\"Gambit also accepts dht: with memory backing.\\\"\n                            \\\"WebSocket serving and signed DHT names and heads are unavailable.\\\"])))\\\"\\\"\\\")\np.write_text(s)\n\np = Path(\\\"host/gambit/ffi/README.md\\\")\ns = p.read_text()\nstart, end = s.index(\\\"\"'`make gambitdht`\"), s.index(\"The real collector\", s.index(\"`make gambitdht`\"))\ns = s[:start] + \"\"\"`make gambitdht` exercises the memory-backed `dht:` session, the DHT\nrequest ring and the native UDP loopback. `make gambitdht-durable` opens\nboth `file:<dir>` and `dht:<dir>`, checks a second launch is refused while\nthe writer owns the directory, waits for a second UDP peer to read a\nreplicated value and verifies the bytes and HEAD in new Yin processes\nresuming from `state.edn`. Pass `DATOMWORLD_ROOT` when the checkouts are\nnot siblings.\n\nYin uses Gambit file ports for the Jing content log, native metadata\nfile reads, exclusive temporary writes and rename. `force-output` at\nlevel 1 supplies POSIX `fsync` for open file ports. Directory creation,\nclassification and canonical directory resolution use Gambit'\"'\\\\''s filesystem\nprimitives. The directory lock uses \"'`fcntl(F_SETLK)` with the same whole-file\nrecord lock as Chez. Lock open and close, recovery truncation, directory\nsync and writability checks run on a private native worker. The bridge\nonly submits and polls these jobs, and Gambit parks between polls. The\nworker owns C memory and enters no Scheme code. Public `:blocking` FFI\ncontinues to refuse. Gambit'\"'\\\\''s Yin adapter still lacks WebSocket serving\nand signed DHT names and heads.\n\n\"'`host/gambit/yin/datomworld-launcher.patch` updates the Datomworld\n`bb yin-repl` capability banner and manual for a checkout using this\nruntime.\n\n\"\"\" + s[end:]\np.write_text(s)\n'\"'\ngit diff --check\nsh -n test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh\npython3 -c 'import ast; from pathlib import Path; ast.parse(Path(\\\"test/gambit/yin-dht-durable.py\\\").read_text())'\nsed -n '128,182p' host/gambit/yin/file.ss\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
